& [Status]
  + [implementation] complete_against_exact_Slice9_phase_lock
  + [authority] consumed_and_closed

& [CustodyForms]
  + NativeLifecycleCustodyHandle binds exact request identity operation and normalized request SHA256 digest
  + NativeLifecycleCustodyEntry retains the complete typed request byte account exact handle and domain-separated entry digest
  + NativeLifecycleCustodyRegistry is one strict immutable BTreeMap with exact count retained-byte account root digest and fixed nonclaims

& [Operations]
  + new returns one replay-valid empty registry
  + compile_handle bounds and normalizes a typed request without deciding its lifecycle outcome
  + register validates the entire predecessor returns a successor value and refuses duplicate digests without overwrite
  + resolve validates the entire registry and exact supplied handle before returning the retained request
  + validate_from_custody resolves then delegates once to the unchanged Slice7 validator

& [Bounds]
  + at most eight entries eight megabytes per normalized request and sixty-four megabytes aggregate retained request bytes
  + unknown fields malformed digests key drift count drift byte drift root drift entry drift and handle substitution fail closed
  + equivalent insertion sets produce byte-equivalent registries independent of insertion order

& [HonestyAndSecurity]
  + the digest is a locator commitment and never reconstructs omitted meaning
  + refused lifecycle requests may be retained and remain refused because custody does not reinterpret them
  + no digest registry or successful lookup claims truth correctness safety authentication authorization signature permission or later lifecycle authority
  + no hidden mutation persistence expiry eviction provider model filesystem process network clock environment remote or external effect exists

& [Rollback]
  + remove the lifecycle custody module export focused tests and Slice9 completion records
  + retain Slice7 validation Slice8 MCP and all preserved Slice9 source SJS canonical justification plan matrix and phase lock records
